# Jenkins CI/CD Project -- Git Integration (Beginner to Intermediate)

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the implementation of a **Continuous
Integration (CI) pipeline** using **Jenkins** integrated with
**GitHub**.\
The pipeline automatically pulls source code from a Git repository and
executes build steps using Jenkins.

The project is designed to showcase **hands-on Jenkins experience**
suitable for **entry-level to junior DevOps roles**.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Architecture Flow

Developer → GitHub Repository → Jenkins Server → Build Execution →
Console Output

------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Tools & Technologies Used

-   **Jenkins** -- Continuous Integration server\
-   **Git & GitHub** -- Version control and source code management\
-   **Linux (Ubuntu)** -- Jenkins host OS\
-   **Shell Scripting** -- Build execution\
-   **Java 21** -- Jenkins runtime

------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Key Features

-   Jenkins installation and configuration
-   Git plugin integration
-   Freestyle Jenkins job creation
-   Source code pulled from GitHub
-   Shell-based build execution
-   Build logs verification via Jenkins console output

------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Prerequisites

-   Ubuntu 20.04 / 22.04
-   Java 21 installed
-   Git installed
-   Jenkins installed and running
-   GitHub account

